  "title": "The Freewheelin' Bob Dylan",
  "country": "US",
  "released": "1963-05-27",
  "notes": "Mono first pressing on Columbia red \"2-Eye\" labels with \"Guaranteed High Fidelity\" at bottom. \n\n\"P\" stamped in runouts denotes [l=Columbia Records Pressing Plant, Pitman], pressing. Remainder of runouts mostly stamped, plating hashes etched.\n\nBack liner variation, with \"6\" fabrication code, and both Monaural (CL 1986) and Stereo (CS 8786) catalog numbers.\n\nSome copies with hype sticker:\nSinging His Sensational Hit \"Blowin' In The Wind\"\n\nThe liner notes mistakenly credit the following musicians on track B1: [a=Bruce Langhorne] (guitar), [a=George Barnes] (bass guitar), [a=Dick Wellstood] (piano), [a=Gene Ramey] (bass), and [url=/artist/343297]Herb Lovelle[/url] (drums).\n\n© Columbia Records 1963",
  "released_formatted": "27 May 1963",
